USER: Yes. [Implement it.]

CLAUDE: Read experiment.py and config.py. Discovered the resume feature is already implemented: default behavior detects incomplete experiments and prompts to resume; --restart forces regeneration. However, found a latent bug: find_completed_iterations() passed the unsanitized actual_model name to the glob pattern (e.g. "deepseek-r1:8b"), but generate_filename() writes files with sanitize_model_name() applied (e.g. "deepseekr18b"). The glob never matched existing files for any model with punctuation in its name — which is effectively all models. Fixed by adding model_name = sanitize_model_name(model_name) inside find_completed_iterations() before the glob. Logged bug in claude_errors.log.

