USER: What is causing summarize.py to skip the file results\20260609190147-animals_big-animals_hard-fh-deepseekr18b-t01-19.yml?

CLAUDE: Read the file and traced the full processing path through summarize.py. The model returned YAML with the list wrapped under a named key (- animals: [list]). yaml.safe_load produced [{animals: [...]}]. parse_yaml's list branch set items = data but the existing YAML-Single-List-Flattening check only fires when items[0] is a list, not a dict. The dict reached process_and_track, was str()-converted by trim_items, flagged by detect_preamble_leak (6+ words), and filtered out entirely — 0 items, silent. File appeared in zero_item_files, not skipped_trials.

